// Committed, shared build settings.
//
// Signing identity is deliberately NOT here — a team ID identifies an Apple Developer
// account and does not belong in a shared repository. It lives in Config/Local.xcconfig,
// which is gitignored. The `?` makes the include optional, so a fresh clone still builds
// and tests on the simulator (which needs no signing) without any local setup.

// Build-time default for the coach's Ollama address, baked into Info.plist. Empty here on
// purpose: a LAN address is personal, and this file is committed.
//
// Write it WITHOUT a scheme — "10.0.0.99:11434", not "http://10.0.0.99:11434". An xcconfig
// treats `//` as a comment, so a URL is silently truncated to "http:" (verified). The app's
// `normalised()` adds the scheme and the default port anyway.
//
// This declaration MUST come BEFORE the include. In an xcconfig the last assignment wins,
// so declaring it afterwards silently overwrote whatever Local.xcconfig set — verified by
// building with a value set and finding an empty string in the built Info.plist.
COACH_DEFAULT_HOST =

#include? "Local.xcconfig"
